&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;About the Role &amp;amp; Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every chart, insight, and experiment result a customer sees in Amplitude passes through the compute layer that this team owns. Our team sits between Amplitude&#39;s front-end analytics products/ rest APIs/ MCPs and Nova, our proprietary analytics database, and owns the compute API that translates a user&#39;s question into a fast, correct answer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mandate: &lt;strong&gt;enable a highly performant, reliable, and flexible way to compute insights.&lt;/strong&gt; Those three goals are often in tension the more flexible we make the system, the harder it is to keep it fast and simple, and a lot of the interesting engineering work on this team lives in that tradeoff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day, you&#39;ll work closely with engineers on data management, marketing analytics, Session Replay, Experiment, CDP, Query, and various product teams, since they&#39;re all consumers of what we build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;As a Senior Software Engineer, you will&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build core parts of the query/compute engine that powers analysis across Amplitude&#39;s product suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the compute API and semantic layer that other engineering teams build features on top of, so that it can support a more generic table&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help unify and evolve our core data model, including how non-event data (profile properties, lookup tables, etc.) is represented alongside event data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the performance, reliability, and scalability of query planning and execution on the Amplitude query engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams across Session Replay, Experiment, CDP, Query, and frontend to understand their needs and shape the compute layer around them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of projects end-to-end, from design through rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;You&#39;ll be a great addition to the team if you have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend or distributed-systems engineering experience, ideally touching OLAP databases, query engines, or data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SQL, query planning/execution, or building APIs that many other engineering teams depend on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort reasoning about tradeoffs between flexibility, performance, and ease of use and making deliberate calls between them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning ambiguous, cross-team projects end-to-end rather than just executing well-scoped tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills; this team&#39;s work only matters in the context of the products built on top of it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus points for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale event or time-series data systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing semantic layers, ORMs, or other data-modeling abstractions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with columnar databases or OLAP query engines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating a data platform with external tools or AI/agent workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Example projects you might work on&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;New compute schema and parallelization&lt;/strong&gt; — redesigning how queries are represented internally to unlock faster, more parallelizable execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deeper session-based analysis&lt;/strong&gt; — extending our session-analysis capabilities with new filters and formula support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Smarter result caching&lt;/strong&gt; — improving both the actual and perceived speed of the query engine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extending SQL as an interface into Amplitude&#39;s data&lt;/strong&gt; lets AI agents, third-party tools, and warehouse-native workflows query Amplitude data directly and reliably. Paving the way for us to run directly on an external warehouse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bringing non-event data into the core model&lt;/strong&gt; — representing things like customer profile properties, sessions, and lookup tables alongside event data, so features can be built against a single consistent model quickly and computed efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data access controls&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp; giving enterprise admins fine-grained control over who can access sensitive data, so they can confidently expand what they send into Amplitude and who can use it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
