&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll work on one of our most critical growth levers — amplitude.com — executing initiatives that support the broader site strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll work on the frontier of AI-powered marketing. We&#39;re actively integrating AI-native workflows across everything we build. And we recently partnered with Statsig to expand our experimentation portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll have dedicated resources: web engineers and brand/growth designers who are aligned to this function — so you can move fast and build with craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll sit within a larger integrated marketing team, giving you exposure across campaigns, product launches, and PLG and sales pipeline initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Amplitude is the category leader in digital analytics and experimentation — and you&#39;ll get hands-on experience running experiments and optimization using the very product we sell.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Growth Marketing Manager you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Website Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own amplitude.com as a growth engine — helping maintain site architecture, user journeys, and content updates that drive both self-serve growth and enterprise pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute against a roadmap grounded in performance data and experimentation insights, flagging opportunities as you spot them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and operate the Sanity CMS platform, supporting other teams across the org as they publish independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversion &amp;amp; Experimentation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and iterate on conversion-focused experiences across product pages, pricing, demo request flows, and campaign landing pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run experiments and track measurement using Amplitude Analytics and Web Experiment to improve engagement, conversion, and pipeline generation across web surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull and organize website-attributed pipeline data in Salesforce, helping surface trends across GTM segments and win/loss patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with web engineering to ship new capabilities — you&#39;re a collaborative teammate in the build process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Marketing, Product, Growth, Sales, and Engineering — communicating clearly and helping move projects forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply repeatable, scalable approaches for product launches and campaign experiences that maintain a high bar for performance and brand consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Native Ways of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement AI-native workflows (Claude, Claude Cowork, Claude Code) to accelerate content creation, site improvements, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At a minimum, you need to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3 years of hands-on experience working on a corporate website or web growth program for a SaaS, AI, or tech company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside engineering teams — you&#39;re comfortable scoping tasks, prioritizing, and collaborating in a technical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experimentation mindset: you&#39;ve helped run A/B tests and conversion optimization efforts on corporate or product marketing sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven by nature — you make decisions from evidence, not intuition alone. Experience with Amplitude or a comparable analytics platform is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a headless CMS (Sanity experience a bonus; Contentful, Prismic, or similar all count).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who can work well with stakeholders across Sales, Product, Engineering, and Marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be a great addition to the team if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a growth-stage startup or scaling SaaS/AI company — you&#39;re comfortable with ambiguity and know how to build systems where none exist.&lt;/li&gt;
