&lt;p&gt;As a Workplace Coordinator, you&#39;ll help make Amplitude&#39;s San Francisco headquarters a place where people want to work. You&#39;ll own the day-to-day operations of our office—from facilities and vendors to supplies, events, and employee experience—while partnering closely with People, IT, Finance, and our Security Coordinator. This is a hands-on role for someone who notices what needs to be done, takes ownership, and can move quickly when priorities change. You&#39;ll report to the Head of Global Workplace and play an important role in keeping our HQ running smoothly and supporting a great in-office experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;As a Workplace Coordinator, you will:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day office and facilities operations, including space readiness, supplies, seating changes, maintenance requests, and coordination with building management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage workplace vendors, invoices, purchase orders, and day-to-day spend while helping ensure services are delivered effectively and within budget.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a great employee experience by coordinating hybrid-day programming, team events, all-hands, celebrations, and executive, customer, and board visits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with IT and People to support new-hire Day 1 logistics, including desk assignments, workstation readiness, office orientation, and badge access coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally on workplace projects, safety preparedness, office communications, and documentation while serving as a go-to resource for employee questions about the office and its amenities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be a great addition to the team if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
