&lt;li&gt;You have a bias toward action and use good judgment to solve problems rather than waiting for someone else to tell you what to do.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly and warmly with everyone from employees and executives to vendors and building partners. Leading with a hospitality white-glove service mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable in a fast-moving environment and stay composed when the office gets busy or plans change at the last minute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited to use technology and AI tools to work smarter and are comfortable with tools like Google Workspace, Slack, and Claude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At a minimum, you need to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in office coordination, workplace operations, facilities, hospitality, or administrative operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing vendors and processing invoices, purchase orders, or similar operational workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple workstreams and follow through from request to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating office events, employee programming, facilities needs, or new hire onboarding logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Google Workspace and Slack, along with the ability to quickly learn new workplace and operational tools.&lt;/li&gt;
